IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa13-ch4-undersubscribed.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 17 Chapter 4 (ss 578 and 579): public companies,
-- allotment where the issue is not fully subscribed. Lines 7872-7894 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of coa13-ch1-shares.l4. Every name begins with the section label it implements.
-- Periods of days are counted from the day after the first making of the offer ("after the first making"): fork F-578.

§ `Part 17, Chapter 4: Public companies: allotment where issue not fully subscribed`

-- ---- s 578: Public companies: allotment where issue not fully subscribed ---------------------------------

-- src:7882 | (4) This section applies in the case of shares offered as wholly or partly payable otherwise than in cash as it applies in the case of shares offered for subscription.
@ref s 578(4) the section applies to shares offered as wholly or partly payable otherwise than in cash (src:7882)
GIVEN `the shares are offered as wholly or partly payable otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(4) section 578 applies to the shares as it applies to shares offered for subscription` MEANS
    IF `the shares are offered as wholly or partly payable otherwise than in cash`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of shares offered as wholly or partly payable otherwise than in cash"

-- src:7874 | (1) No allotment shall be made of shares of a public company offered for subscription unless—
-- src:7875 | (a) the issue is subscribed for in full, or
-- src:7876 | (b) the offer is made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted—
-- src:7877 | (i) in any event, or
-- src:7878 | (ii) if specified conditions are met (and those conditions are met).
@ref s 578(1) no allotment of shares of a public company offered for subscription unless the issue is subscribed in full or the offer is on terms allowing allotment (src:7874-7878)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are offered for subscription` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 578(4) section 578 applies to the shares as it applies to shares offered for subscription` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the issue is subscribed for in full` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted in any event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted if specified conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND (`the shares are offered for subscription` OR `s 578(4) section 578 applies to the shares as it applies to shares offered for subscription` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN IF     `the issue is subscribed for in full`
             OR `the offer is made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted in any event`
             OR (`the offer is made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted if specified conditions are met` AND `those conditions are met`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No allotment shall be made ... unless— (a) the issue is subscribed for in full, or (b) the offer is made on terms that the shares subscribed for may be allotted (i) in any event, or (ii) if specified conditions are met (and those conditions are met)" (the "unless" is met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No allotment shall be made of shares of a public company offered for subscription"

-- src:7879 | (2) If shares are prohibited from being allotted by subsection (1) and 40 days have elapsed after the first making of the offer, all money received from applicants for shares must be repaid to them forthwith, without interest.
@ref s 578(2) if the allotment is prohibited and 40 days have elapsed after the first making of the offer, all money received must be repaid forthwith (src:7879)
GIVEN `s 578(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date of the first making of the offer` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(2) the company must repay the money received from applicants` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 578(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN (`the date of the first making of the offer` PLUS 40)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If shares are prohibited from being allotted by subsection (1) and 40 days have elapsed after the first making of the offer" (the 40 days have not elapsed)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If shares are prohibited from being allotted by subsection (1)" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the shares are prohibited is not known

@ref s 578(2) the money is repaid without interest (src:7879)
GIVEN `s 578(2) the company must repay the money received from applicants` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(2) the company must pay interest on the money repaid under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `s 578(2) the company must repay the money received from applicants` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be repaid to them forthwith, without interest"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without interest" speaks of the repayment under subsection (2)

-- src:7881 | A director is not so liable if he proves that the default in the repayment of the money was not due to any misconduct or negligence on his part.
@ref s 578(3) a director is not liable if he proves the default was not due to his misconduct or negligence (src:7881)
GIVEN `the director proves that the default in the repayment of the money was not due to any misconduct or negligence on his part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(3) the director has the defence in subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the director proves that the default in the repayment of the money was not due to any misconduct or negligence on his part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director is not so liable if he proves that the default ... was not due to any misconduct or negligence on his part" (this section gives no defence on these facts: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:7880 | (3) If any of the money is not repaid within 48 days after the first making of the offer, the directors of the company are jointly and severally liable to repay it, with interest at the rate for the time being specified under section 17 of the Judgments Act 1838 (c. 110) from the expiration of the 48th day.
@ref s 578(3) the directors are jointly and severally liable to repay money not repaid within 48 days, with interest (src:7880)
GIVEN `s 578(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date of the first making of the offer` IS A DATE
      `the money has been repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the money was repaid` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `s 578(3) the director has the defence in subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(3) the director is liable to repay the money, with interest` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 578(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `not repaid within 48 days`
        THEN IF `s 578(3) the director has the defence in subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director is not so liable if he proves that the default in the repayment of the money was not due to any misconduct or negligence on his part"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any of the money is not repaid within 48 days after the first making of the offer" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the money in question is money that must be repaid because the allotment is prohibited (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the shares are prohibited is not known
    WHERE
        `the 48th day after the first making of the offer` MEANS `the date of the first making of the offer` PLUS 48
        `not repaid within 48 days` MEANS
            IF `the money has been repaid`
            THEN `the date on which the money was repaid` GREATER THAN `the 48th day after the first making of the offer`
            ELSE `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the 48th day after the first making of the offer`

@ref s 578(3) interest runs from the expiration of the 48th day after the first making of the offer (src:7880)
GIVEN `the date of the first making of the offer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 578(3) the 48th day after the first making of the offer, from the expiration of which interest runs` MEANS
    `the date of the first making of the offer` PLUS 48

-- src:7883 | (5) In that case—
-- src:7884 | (a) the references in subsection (1) to subscription shall be construed accordingly;
-- src:7885 | (b) references in subsections (2) and (3) to the repayment of money received from applicants for shares include—
-- src:7886 | (i) the return of any other consideration so received (including, if the case so requires, the release of the applicant from any undertaking), or
-- src:7887 | (ii) if it is not reasonably practicable to return the consideration, the payment of money equal to its value at the time it was so received;
-- src:7888 | (c) references to interest apply accordingly.
@ref s 578(5) in a non-cash offer, subscription is construed accordingly, repayment includes returning other consideration, and interest applies accordingly (src:7883-7888)
GIVEN `section 578 applies to the shares under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(5)(a) the references in subsection (1) to subscription are construed accordingly` MEANS
    IF `section 578 applies to the shares under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In that case— (a) the references in subsection (1) to subscription shall be construed accordingly"

@ref s 578(5)(c) references to interest apply accordingly (src:7888)
GIVEN `section 578 applies to the shares under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(5)(c) the references to interest apply accordingly` MEANS
    IF `section 578 applies to the shares under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In that case— ... (c) references to interest apply accordingly"

DECLARE `s 578(5)(b) way in which the applicant's consideration is repaid` IS ONE OF
    `s 578(5)(b)(i) the consideration is returned (and, if the case so requires, the applicant is released from any undertaking)`
    `s 578(5)(b)(ii) money is paid equal to the value of the consideration at the time it was received` HAS `amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 578(5)(b) the consideration was money, so the subsection adds nothing`

@ref s 578(5)(b) repayment includes returning any other consideration, or paying its value if not reasonably practicable (src:7885-7887)
GIVEN `the consideration received from the applicant was other than money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonably practicable to return the consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the consideration at the time it was received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 578(5)(b) way in which the applicant's consideration is repaid`
`s 578(5)(b) the applicant's consideration is repaid by` MEANS
    IF `the consideration received from the applicant was other than money`
    THEN IF `it is reasonably practicable to return the consideration`
         THEN `s 578(5)(b)(i) the consideration is returned (and, if the case so requires, the applicant is released from any undertaking)`
         ELSE `s 578(5)(b)(ii) money is paid equal to the value of the consideration at the time it was received` `the value of the consideration at the time it was received`
    ELSE `s 578(5)(b) the consideration was money, so the subsection adds nothing`

-- src:7889 | (6) Any condition requiring or binding an applicant for shares to waive compliance with any requirement of this section is void.
@ref s 578(6) a condition binding an applicant to waive compliance with the section is void (src:7889)
GIVEN `the condition requires or binds an applicant for shares to waive compliance with a requirement of section 578` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 578(6) the condition is void` MEANS
    IF `the condition requires or binds an applicant for shares to waive compliance with a requirement of section 578`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any condition requiring or binding an applicant for shares to waive compliance with any requirement of this section is void"

-- ---- s 579: Public companies: effect of irregular allotment where issue not fully subscribed ------------

-- src:7891 | (1) An allotment made by a public company to an applicant in contravention of section 578 (public companies: allotment where issue not fully subscribed) is voidable at the instance of the applicant within one month after the date of the allotment, and not later.
@ref s 579(1) an allotment in contravention of s 578 is voidable at the instance of the applicant within one month after the date of the allotment, and not later (src:7891)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment was made to an applicant in contravention of section 578` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the applicant avoids the allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579(1) the allotment is voidable at the instance of the applicant` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `the allotment was made to an applicant in contravention of section 578`
    THEN IF `the date on which the applicant avoids the allotment` AT MOST (`add months` `the date of the allotment` 1)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "voidable at the instance of the applicant within one month after the date of the allotment, and not later"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An allotment made by a public company to an applicant in contravention of section 578"

-- src:7892 | (2) It is so voidable even if the company is in the course of being wound up.
@ref s 579(2) it is so voidable even if the company is in the course of being wound up (src:7892)
GIVEN `the company is in the course of being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579(2) the allotment is voidable although the company is being wound up` MEANS
    IF `the company is in the course of being wound up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "even if the company is in the course of being wound up"

-- src:7893 | (3) A director of a public company who knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises the contravention of, any provision of section 578 with respect to allotment is liable to compensate the company and the allottee respectively for any loss, damages, costs or expenses that the company or allottee may have sustained or incurred by the contravention.
@ref s 579(3) a director who knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises the contravention of, s 578 is liable to compensate the company and the allottee (src:7893)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises the contravention of, a provision of section 578 with respect to allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579(3) the director is liable to compensate the company and the allottee` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `the director knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises the contravention of, a provision of section 578 with respect to allotment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A director of a public company who knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises the contravention of, any provision of section 578"

@ref s 579(3) the loss the company or the allottee may have sustained or incurred (src:7893)
GIVEN `the loss, damages, costs or expenses that the company or allottee may have sustained or incurred by the contravention` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 579(3) the amount the director is liable to compensate the company or the allottee` MEANS
    `the loss, damages, costs or expenses that the company or allottee may have sustained or incurred by the contravention`

-- src:7894 | (4) Proceedings to recover any such loss, damages, costs or expenses may not be brought more than two years after the date of the allotment.
@ref s 579(4) proceedings to recover the loss may not be brought more than two years after the date of the allotment (src:7894)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the proceedings are brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 579(4) the proceedings may be brought` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the proceedings are brought` GREATER THAN (`add years` `the date of the allotment` 2)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be brought more than two years after the date of the allotment"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars proceedings after two years and does not grant a right to bring them within it
